A||N||7||Rob Durham||Wheels , need help, PLEASE||||7||
Z||000000||Rob Durham||04-25-2001||03:12 PM||||Hi, this seems like a cool forum, do you guys take well to newbee's??<P>I just got an 87 GT fastback and am looking for wheels and tires, can a 16" or 17" wheel be used if so what is the widest I could go(without looking stupid) and what would the offset need to be, I want something that will be extreamly low profile but compleatly fill up the wheel opening.<P>Thanks in advance,<BR>Rob<P>||||reg||7
Z||000001||fierojunky||04-25-2001||03:22 PM||||Welcome to the forum - i am not the person to answer your question.  However, the forum does have a search feature and you might find some info that way.  Your going to have to lower your car about 1.5" to close the gap in the wheel well.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000002||ferg||04-25-2001||04:00 PM||||Welcome to the forum. <P>Go to tirerack.com - you can do a search of your car and see lots of different options for wheels. <P>To answer your question - yes 16's and 17's can be used. I don't know the offset- but I think I remember seeing 7" as being the widest you could go.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroLisa||04-25-2001||05:14 PM||||I do believe the correct offset is 5x100 but I'm pulling that out of my hazy memory...<P>Like someone said, 17s can easily be used, I have them on my car, with still lots of room to lower. I've seen 18's used too.. no mods to the car required.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||04-25-2001||05:49 PM||||Welcome to the Forum!<P>I've seen a couple with 18's on them.  They looked good, but I'd rather go with a 17 and lower the car to eliminate the gaps in the wheel wells.  Although, I am not sure how much lower I would want the Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>Don't worry about being a new member on this board.  You will find everyone here very friendly and informative!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black88GT||04-25-2001||05:52 PM||||5x100 is the bolt pattern.  I'm not sure about the offset either, but I can guarantee you if you search for it you will find it, there is a 50 post tire size thread every other week...||||reg||1
Z||000006||Rob Durham||04-25-2001||08:01 PM||||Thanks EVERYONE!<P>I can see you guys are going to be a BIG help, I will be hanging around here alot!<P>Rob||||reg||7
Z||000007||Wannabe||04-25-2001||09:20 PM||||For the '87 GT, the wheels are 7 wide by 15 diameter. 5 x 100mm bolt pattern and 35mm offset. You can go with a larger diameter (16 or 17") and the same width without changing the offset, but if you go wider, you may want to go with more offset to keep the tires from sticking out past the fender opening, particularly in front.<p>[This message has been edited by Wannabe (edited 04-25-2001).]||||reg||1
